      "id": "synchronous-transfer",
      "text": "On a fresh pipe, start Write with five bytes and keep both ends open. A Read with a two-byte buffer returns the first two bytes and nil. The writer acknowledges that count and waits with three bytes left. A second Read with room for at least three bytes returns the remainder and nil, and Write returns (5, nil). The returned reader is the writer's embedded reader, so both ends use the same unbuffered channels. A competing Write cannot interleave bytes while the first holds the write mutex.",
      "citation": {
