      "id": "one-sided-close-and-repeat",
      "text": "On a fresh pipe, close only the writer with a non-nil error W, then close it again with a different error. Both calls return nil, and a subsequent Read returns (0, W) with the original error value. If the first call was plain Close, the Read returns (0, EOF) even after a later CloseWithError. In the mirror case, closing only the reader preserves its first custom error for subsequent Writes, with ErrClosedPipe stored by plain Close. An operation on the end that was itself closed returns (0, ErrClosedPipe).",
      "citation": {
        "line": 24,
